{
 "id": "the-drowned-testament",
 "name": "The Drowned Testament",
 "tagline": "Water and restricted movement",
 "identity": "The Drowned Testament was once Aurelia's largest coastal city. When the sea reclaimed the lowlands, its streets became canals, its plazas became shallow lakes, and its towers became isolated islands of stone. The old city is still recognisable from above: a network of flooded avenues, raised districts, bridges and drowned courtyards. The surviving dry ground is extremely valuable because it determines where armies can move and where towers can be constructed. This map is less about occupying open territory and more about controlling access between separated districts.",
